ove the visible area — many simple implementations do that. Keep simple: spawn collision → game over. Also, when locking, if any cell is above row 0 and the piece is \"committed\"... I'll just do spawn collision, plus if after lock there are cells in row 0 only... hmm. Let me do: after locking, if piece's minimum y cell < 0? That means it partially went above. Common approach: game over if the piece locks with cells above the top AND it's not possible... Simplest robust: check game over at spawn time. That works fine.\n\nWall kicks for rotation: try [0,0], [-1,0], [1,0], [0,-1], [-2,0], [2,0], [0,1]. Simple offsets rotation:\n\n```js\nfunction tryRotate(dir) {\n  const rotated = dir>0 ? rotate(piece.matrix) : rotateCCW(piece.matrix);\n  for (const [dx,dy] of [{dx:0,dy:0},{dx:-1,dy:0},{dx:1,dy:0},{dx:0,dy:-1},{dx:-2,dy:0},{dx:2,dy:0},{dx:0,dy:1}]) {\n    if (!collide(rotated, piece.x+dx, piece.y+dy)) { piece.matrix=rotated; piece.x+=dx; piece.y+=dy; return; }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nGame loop with rAF:\n\n```js\nlet lastTime=0, dropAcc=0;\nfunction loop(t) {\n  requestAnimationFrame(loop);\n  if (!playing) { lastTime=t; return; }\n  const dt = t-lastTime; lastTime=t;\n  dropAcc += dt;\n  const interval = softDrop ? 40 : getFallInterval();\n  while (dropAcc >= interval) {\n    dropAcc -= interval;\n    step();\n  }\n}\n```\n\nActually soft drop should be triggered by holding down key. Track keys pressed. Let me track `softDropping` boolean set by down key keydown/keyup.\n\nFall interval: based on level: `Math.max(100, 800 * Math.pow(0.85, level-1))` or similar. e.g., level 1: 800ms, decreasing.\n\nScoring: 1: 100*level? Common: 1 line 100, 2 300, 3 500, 4 800, multiplied by level. I'll do base * (level).\n\nLine clear animation: mark cleared rows, flash white for ~250ms, then collapse. Nice touch. During animation, pause gravity (sets a state). Let me implement: on lock, find full rows, if any, set state 'clearing', flash timer, then remove rows and decrement scores. Manageab